        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "CYCLOPHOSPHAMIDE:\n  Prodrug: activated by CYP2B6/3A4 → phosphoramide mustard (active alkylator) + acrolein\n  Use: lymphomas, autoimmune (lupus nephritis, vasculitis), HSCT conditioning\n  Acrolein → hemorrhagic cystitis → must co-administer MESNA (2-mercaptoethane sulfonate Na)\n    or aggressive hydration to prevent bladder toxicity\n  Myelosuppression, alopecia, teratogenic, secondary malignancies (leukemia 5–10yr later)\n  SIADH at high doses"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-CANCER-DRUGS.md#012",
      "path": [
        "06-CANCER-DRUGS.md"
